---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import CourseCalendar from "../../components/CourseCalendar.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../../course-config";
import { formatCourseDate } from "../../lib/dates";
import { siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Calendar"
  description={`The whole of ${courseMeta.session}, ${courseMeta.year} on one page: ${formatCourseDate(courseMeta.startDate)} to ${formatCourseDate(courseMeta.endDate)}.`}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <CourseCalendar />

  <p>
    The three lists this page gathers &mdash; lectures, seminars, assessment
    &mdash; each read as though the course ran at a steady rate. Side by side
    they don't. The seminar column is empty more often than it is full, and the
    weeks it skips are the ones the syllabus wanted you spending on the work
    rather than on the argument about the work. Read the gaps as content: a
    week with nothing scheduled in it is the only way a course about
    subtraction can practise what it teaches on its own timetable.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
